203ea6762b:
Broccolini is a family-owned, single-source provider of construction, development and real-estate services. Our company caters to the industrial, commercial and residential markets in Canada. Recognized for our quality workmanship, innovative technology, open collaboration, and exceptional standards, we offer a one-stop approach to the planning, development and construction of remarkable buildings. We are currently looking for a Field Coordinator to join our Toronto team!
 RESPONSIBILITIES 
 Act as the liaison between the Site Superintendent and trade labour force;
 Maintain the daily construction log in conjunction with the Site Superintendent;
 Prepare and maintain various site communication/documentation with head office and site;
 Prepare and maintain various files for purchaser agreements (PA);
 Coordinate municipal inspections, Tarion and/or professional inspections;
 Maintain familiarity with WHMIS, WSIB and OHS safety responsibilities and duties;
 Attend and participate in site meetings, prepare meeting agendas, record meeting minutes and prepare them for distribution as directed;
 Conduct physical checks on the labour force and record individual activity on time sheets;
 Calculate labour hours per activity and submit time sheets to the office;
 Obtain labour requirements from the Site Superintendent and coordinate sign-on of labourers when required;
 Allocate daily tasks to labourers according to the Site Superintendent's instructions;
 Order supplies according to requirements and submit requisitions for non-standard items to the purchaser;
 Arrange for supplies to be delivered and compare delivery notes against the bill of quantities and actual quantities delivered;
 Check material requested versus quantity allowed, and maintain inventory of required materials;
 Coordinate incoming and outgoing shipments, including temporary storage on site.
 QUALIFICATIONS 
 Post-secondary diploma in Engineering, Architecture or equivalent;
 A minimum of 3 years' experience in a similar role;
 Strong knowledge of the construction field;
 Exceptional communication and organizational skills;
 Ability to meet deadlines, manage time effectively and work in a fast-paced environment;
 Excellent knowledge of MS Office; tech-savvy with various computer software.
 WHAT WE OFFER 
 Broccolini is a fast-growing company that offers a multi-market approach, a dynamic working environment, a competitive compensation program and excellent benefits such as:
 Group Insurance Plan (three plans to choose from)
 Telemedicine (24/7 access to a nurse or doctor)
 Employee Assistance Program
 Professional Training & Development Program
 Mentorship Program
 An active social & wellness committee
 Broccolini thanks all interested applicants; however, only those under consideration will be contacted. 
 Broccolini is an equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability status or veteran status. Accommodations for applicants with disabilities are available at all stages of the recruitment process upon request. Broccolini uses artificial intelligence tools to help screen and assess applications. All hiring decisions are made by our People & Culture team and hiring managers.

